# Health endpoint contract — PCS-3932
# Each block below is a self-contained HTTP exchange. The `=== expect ===`
# section is the acceptance criterion for the request immediately above.

### Case 1: GET /health → 200 JSON {"status":"ok"}
GET /health HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000
Accept: application/json

=== expect ===
status: 200
header Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
header Content-Length: 15
body: {"status":"ok"}

### Case 2: GET /health/ (trailing slash) → same as Case 1 per FR-004
GET /health/ HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000

=== expect ===
status: 200
header Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
body: {"status":"ok"}

### Case 3: HEAD /health → 200 headers, empty body
HEAD /health HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000

=== expect ===
status: 200
header Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
body: (empty)

### Case 4: POST /health → 405 with Allow header
POST /health HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000
Content-Length: 0

=== expect ===
status: 405
header Allow: GET, HEAD

### Case 5: GET /nope → 404
GET /nope HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000

=== expect ===
status: 404
